{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>YHWH your Elohim, He, etc. He will destroy, etc.</b> It was necessary to say הוּא (\"He\") twice and not suffice with one. The intention is to comfort them concerning his passing, and that they would lack two great and precious things: first, that they had in him a shield before YHWH, so that they would not be destroyed — as we find in the incident of the calf and of the spies, were it not for Moses His chosen one. Second, that it was he who destroyed and shattered the two kings of the Amorites, Sihon and Og, and who would arise in his place to fight the great battles that lay ahead of them?" "<b>Therefore</b> he said: concerning what pertains to YHWH he said, ״YHWH your Elohim, He passes before you״ — in the manner of what He said (Exodus 17:5): ״Pass before the people״ — meaning, that He is the one who passes over your transgression, and to Him you should hold fast for good and not to me. For so we find that He stirred the spirit of Moses to pray for them in the incident of the calf, as it is written (Exodus 32:10): ״Leave Me,״ etc. And there is no loss in Moses' absence regarding the passing over of transgression, for He Himself will pass before you." "<b>And corresponding to</b> the might of battle he said: for it is not the strength of Moses that accomplishes valor, but YHWH is the one who wages war, and that is what he said: ״He will destroy,״ etc. And regarding the intermediary, he said: ״Joshua, he passes before you.״" "<b>And he was precise</b> to say הוּא (\"he\"). This may be explained along the lines of what the prophet said in the battle of Ai: when thirty-six men of Israel fell and Joshua fell on his face, YHWH said to him: ״Arise, why is it that you are falling on your face?״ (Joshua 7:10). And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 44a) that YHWH said to him: ״You caused it, for you did not go out with them.״ And that is what Moses said: ״He passes״ — meaning, the matter depends on his going himself before you and not his emissary."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:46.374098984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}